course: dictionary
lesson: 13708
title: Words that spark ideas
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Inspiration is a feeling or idea that starts something new in your mind. «The sunset over the lake gave her inspiration for her painting.» The sunset gave her ideas, so inspiration here means the ideas that come from something you see, hear or feel.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Our gymnastics coach is an inspiration to us all» tells you that a person can be an inspiration too. The sentence says the coach makes everyone want to do well. Ask yourself: what does this sentence say the coach does?
explain: Sometimes inspiration comes all at once. «Ruby had a flash of inspiration and knew how the story would end.» A flash is very quick, so inspiration here means a sudden good idea. Swap in «a sudden good idea» and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Inspiration means a sudden good idea, or something that gives you ideas for writing, art or music.
fact: «An inspiration» can also be a person or thing that makes you want to do well or be like them.
fact: Inspiration is usually uncountable: we say «she found inspiration», not «she found an inspiration».
fact: Useful phrases: «a source of inspiration», «draw inspiration from», «a flash of inspiration».
fact: In science, inspiration means breathing in.
exercise: «The sunset over the lake gave her inspiration for her painting.» What does inspiration mean here? | Going to bed early | *A sudden idea that helped her create something | A cold wind off the water | A tin of paint
exercise: «Our gymnastics coach is an inspiration to us all.» What does an inspiration mean here? | A loud noise | A long rest after training | A kind of sports ball | *Someone who makes us want to do well
exercise: «Ruby had a flash of inspiration and knew how the story would end.» Find and copy one word that shows the idea came suddenly. | *flash | story | knew | ending
test: «Her sad song gave me inspiration for a story about a lost dog.» What does inspiration mean here? | A small drum | Going out to play | *Ideas that help you create something | A bad mood
test: Which phrase means you got your ideas from something you saw or heard? | break the ice | *draw inspiration from | take a nap | give up
exam: Mia says, «Mrs Hall is an inspiration.» What does Mia mean? | Mrs Hall is always late | *Mrs Hall makes Mia want to do well and be like her | Mrs Hall is a new student | Mrs Hall is very loud
